{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מי ומי ההולכים", :translit "mi u'mi ha'holkhim", :gloss "who and who are the ones going"} {:he "מי ומי ההלכים", :translit "mi u'mi hahalkhim", :gloss "who and who are the ones going"} {:he "כלב ובן נון", :translit "kalev u'ven nun", :gloss "Caleb and son of Nun"} {:he "בנערינו ובזקנינו נלך", :translit "b'ne'areinu uvizkeineinu nelekh", :gloss "with our young and with our old we will go"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מי ומי ההלכים", :b "כלב ובן נון"}], :frame {:text "Pharaoh mocks Moses by suggesting that since the entire generation that left Egypt is decreed to die in the wilderness, only Joshua and Caleb would survive to enter the land — so 'who are the ones going?' Moses replies 'with our young and with our old we will go,' because the decree of dying in the wilderness applied only to those between twenty and sixty years old: the decree was pronounced on those counted from age twenty upward (Numbers 14:29), and none over sixty at the Exodus were included among those decreed, as the count was of fighting-age men (Numbers 1:3, Numbers 14:29).", :sources ["Numbers 14:29" "Numbers 1:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "מי ומי ההלכים", :a-value 216, :b "כלב ובן נון", :b-value 216, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:14:42.896549911Z", :model "glm-5.2"}